  "id": "nagpuri_jhumair",
  "name": "Nagpuri jhumair (Chotanagpur folk song-dance)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Nagpuri song, sung in the Sadri language, is the shared folk music of the Chotanagpur plateau around Ranchi, with forms that follow the farming and festival year, among them jhumair, the domkach wedding dance and the songs of the karam festival. Men and women dance jhumair in linked lines to the mandar barrel drum, the nagara kettledrum and the bamboo flute; here a generic membrane drum card stands in for the mandar. Mukund Nayak carried the style to the stage and to recordings.",
